TITLE:: SuperDirtGUI
summary:: extra synths, effects and sample helpers for SuperDirt, loaded into a running instance
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirt, Classes/DirtOrbit, Classes/GlobalDirtEffect, Classes/DirtModule

DESCRIPTION::
A loader that reads three folders of plain code::.scd:: files - code::synths/::,
code::modules/:: and code::effects/:: next to its own code::classes/:: folder -
into a link::Classes/SuperDirt:: you already run. SuperDirt itself is never
changed, so this lives next to a normal install and updates on its own.

code::
s.boot;
~dirt = SuperDirt(2, s);
~dirt.loadSoundFiles;
~dirt.start(57120, 0 ! 12);
~sdg = SuperDirtGUI(~dirt);
~sdg.gui;
::

Every file is loaded the way SuperDirt loads its own code::synths/:: folder,
with code::~dirt:: bound to the instance and code::~sdg:: to this loader, in
alphabetical order. Each folder ships one example file that is a template: copy
it, rename it, edit it.

table::
## strong::folder:: || strong::one file holds:: || strong::switched on from Tidal by::
## code::synths/:: || a SynthDef in SuperDirt's argument convention || code::s "sdgsine"::
## code::modules/:: || code::~dirt.addModule(name, func, test):: and its SynthDef, code::"name" ++ ~dirt.numChannels:: || the parameter its test looks for
## code::effects/:: || code::SynthDef("global_name" ++ ~dirt.numChannels):: and code::~sdg.addGlobalEffect(\global_name, [\params]):: || one of its parameters
::

subsection:: Who owns what

Synths are added to link::Classes/SynthDescLib::.global and sent to the
server; they stay there after link::#-free::, since Tidal may still be playing
them. Modules are added to code::~dirt.modules:: and removed by
link::#-free:: and link::#-reload::. Global effects are one
link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect:: per orbit, put first in the orbit's chain,
ahead of SuperDirt's delay and reverb; link::#-free:: releases them and hands
the orbits back the way they were.

Orbits exist only after code::~dirt.start::, so make the loader after
code::start::. Made before, it loads synths and modules at once and adds the
global effects on its own once the orbits appear. After a later
code::~dirt.stop; ~dirt.start(...):: call link::#-applyGlobalEffects::
yourself: new orbits do not know about us.

subsection:: Files that fail

A file with an error in it is reported with a warning and skipped; the other
files still load. Fix it and link::#-reload::.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Make the loader and load everything.
ARGUMENT:: dirt
the link::Classes/SuperDirt:: to load into, usually code::~dirt::.
RETURNS:: a SuperDirtGUI.

METHOD:: current
The loader made last, or nil after it was freed.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: load
Read all three folders. Called by code::new::.

METHOD:: reload
Take our modules and global effects out, then read every file again. Edited a
file? This is what to call - no reboot, no recompile.

METHOD:: loadSynths
METHOD:: loadModules
METHOD:: loadGlobalEffects
One folder each.

METHOD:: synthNames
METHOD:: moduleNames
METHOD:: globalEffectNames
What the three folders added, as Symbols, in load order.

METHOD:: addGlobalEffect
Called from a file in code::effects/::. Registers a SynthDef name and the event
keys it listens to; link::#-applyGlobalEffects:: then gives every orbit an
instance.
ARGUMENT:: name
the SynthDef name without the channel count, e.g. code::\global_sdgspace::.
ARGUMENT:: paramNames
an Array of Symbols: the Tidal parameters that wake the effect and are passed on.
ARGUMENT:: alwaysRun
true to keep it awake even when no parameter arrives. false by default.

METHOD:: applyGlobalEffects
Give every orbit its own link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect:: for each registered
name, first in the chain, and rebuild the node tree. An orbit that already has
one is left alone, so calling it twice changes nothing. Waits for the server
once, since code::SynthDef.add:: is asynchronous.

METHOD:: globalEffectSpecs
The registered specs, one Event per effect: code::name::, code::paramNames::,
code::alwaysRun::.

METHOD:: loadSamples
Append a folder of sample banks to the sound library: one bank per subfolder,
files numbered by name, the way Dirt-Samples is laid out. Banks already loaded
stay.
ARGUMENT:: folderPath
a String; code::~:: is expanded.

METHOD:: gui
Open the window, or bring it to the front: three lists of what is loaded, a
reload button and a free button.
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Window::.

METHOD:: window
The window while it is open, nil otherwise.

METHOD:: free
Take our modules and global effects out of code::~dirt::, forget the names and
close the window. Synths stay on the server.

METHOD:: dirt
The link::Classes/SuperDirt:: this loads into.

METHOD:: path
The repository folder, found from the class file. Works through the
extensions symlink and for a quark install alike.

METHOD:: synthDir
METHOD:: moduleDir
METHOD:: effectDir
The three folders.

METHOD:: verbose
METHOD:: verbose_
Whether to post one line per file loaded. true by default.


EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;

(
s.waitForBoot {
	~dirt = SuperDirt(2, s);
	~dirt.loadSoundFiles;
	s.sync;
	~dirt.start(57120, 0 ! 12);
	s.sync;
	~sdg = SuperDirtGUI(~dirt);
};
)

~sdg.synthNames;           // -> [ sdgsine ]
~sdg.moduleNames;          // -> [ sdgcomb ]
~sdg.globalEffectNames;    // -> [ global_sdgspace ]
~sdg.gui;

// from tidal:
//   d1 $ s "sdgsine" # n "0 7 12"
//   d1 $ s "bd*4" # pF "sdgcomb" 0.4
//   d1 $ s "bd*4" # pF "sdgspace" 0.5

// the same event from sclang, without tidal
~dirt.orbits[0].valuePairs([\s, \sdgsine, \n, 7, \sdgcomb, 0.4, \sdgspace, 0.5]);

// edited a file in synths/, modules/ or effects/
~sdg.reload;

// done
~sdg.free;
::

There is a startup you can evaluate a block at a time in
code::examples/superdirt-gui-demo.scd:: in the repository.
